# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
post_install() {
    cat <<'MSG'

  macbook91-cs4208 installed.

  Apply the card policy and reboot:

      systemctl --user restart wireplumber
      sudo reboot

  Then check the result. The tool asks a few questions and returns one
  PASS/FAIL; on failure it writes a single diagnostic archive.

      macbook91-audio-verify

  WHAT THE WIREPLUMBER RULE DOES, AND WHY IT IS NOT OPTIONAL

  Software volume. The internal speaker path has no hardware volume
  control, so without the rule the volume slider does nothing and output
  stays at full scale. macbook91-audio-verify FAILs loudly if it did not
  take effect.

  Its own ACP profile set. This card has exactly one usable analog output
  profile, and the stock profile set drops that profile's only port while
  headphones are plugged - the desktop then shows "Dummy Output" and there
  is no sound at all, from speakers or headphones. The driver moves the
  stream to the headphone converter itself, so the port must stay.

  The speakers appear as a 4-channel device ("Analog Surround 4.0"): the
  four internal amplifiers sit on four TDM slots, measured as two stereo
  pairs rather than a surround layout. Stereo content is copied to both
  pairs, so it reaches all four amplifiers.

  Speakers survive a deep suspend, confirmed on hardware
  across five suspends in one day, the longest 1 h 44 min.

  To roll back completely:   pacman -R macbook91-cs4208-dkms, then reboot

  KERNEL SERIES

MSG
    printf '  The module is built for kernels of Linux series %s.\n' \
        "$(/usr/lib/macbook91-cs4208/kernel-series --list 2>/dev/null || echo '(unknown: the series list could not be read)')"
    cat <<'MSG'
  DKMS skips every other kernel, which keeps its stock codec and has no
  speaker output; after every kernel installation a WARNING names each
  installed kernel of another series. Boot the LTS kernel for audio until
  the package supports that series.

  The CachyOS LTS kernel (linux-cachyos-lts) is the default this package
  depends on. Install linux-cachyos-headers to have the module built for
  the current CachyOS kernel as well.

MSG
}

# Deliberately the same message: an upgrade shows what an installation shows.
# (Replacing the package's early name macbook91-cs4208 is a removal plus an
# installation, so post_install runs then; measured in an isolated pacman root.)
post_upgrade() { post_install; }
